//! fail
// A function without a body is legal only in an interface file (D9.11, grammar.md section 2),
// so a source file reports one syntax error at its `;`. `main` stands on the same line because
// the bootstrap parser reads it as the missing body and reports a second error at its `fn`.
fn twice(i32 x) i32; fn main() i32 { return 0; } //! error: expected '{', found ';'
